FREAX CHANGELOG
===============

Freax release history, newest first. Entries follow VERSION bumps; the
version number is the single source of truth in the VERSION file.

The 0.5 through 1.08 sections were reconstructed from the complete Git history
of that period. Freax has no Git release tags, so sections follow VERSION
changes and release commits, and unversioned commits are grouped into the
release they built or repaired. Later sections are written as each release
ships.


1.11 - 2026-09-26
------------------
Ctrl+D end-of-input.

- Added Ctrl+D to the kernel line editor with Unix EOF semantics: on an empty
  line it reports EOF and returns false, distinct from the nil used by Ctrl+C;
  with text present it deletes the character under the cursor, or beeps at the
  end of the line.
- The interactive shell now treats EOF as leaving the shell, like logout, so
  the user returns to the login prompt.
- Password prompts ignore Ctrl+D, so an empty password still requires Enter.
- Documented the full line-editing key set in `usr/man/sh`.


1.10 - 2026-09-26
------------------
Shell job control.

- Added background execution with a trailing `&`; each background pipeline is
  one job with one process group.
- Added `jobs`, `fg`, `bg`, and `wait` builtins plus `%n`, `%+`, `%-`, and
  `%prefix` job references.
- Added `kill %JOB` to signal a whole job group.
- Added `$!` for the last background process.
- Every pipeline stage now shares the first stage's process group, so a signal
  or `waitGroup` addresses the pipeline as a unit.
- Added a kernel terminal foreground process group with `setForeground` and
  `getForeground`; a nested shell no longer steals the outer shell's terminal.
- Added Ctrl+Z suspend (TSTP) for the foreground job; Ctrl+C also takes down
  the job's descendants and still falls back to the historical foreground-pid
  walk.
- `wait` and `freax.waitGroup` now report 148 (128 + SIGTSTP) for a suspended
  job instead of blocking forever, so the shell always regains the prompt.
- Background jobs get a closed stdin pipe so they cannot steal terminal input
  until `/dev/null` exists.
- Foreground claims and `spawnIO` group joins are now authorized: an
  unprivileged process may only use its own group or one built from its own
  children with matching uid.
- Job table is bounded and refuses new jobs rather than losing a live one;
  job state uses one process-table snapshot per call instead of one per pid.
- Added `usr/man/jobs`; updated `usr/man/sh` and `usr/man/kill`.
- Added selfcheck coverage for background spawn, `$!`, `wait`, and job exit
  status propagation.


1.09 - 2026-09-26
------------------
M6 baseline measurement and compatibility-contract start.

- Grouped selfcheck output by subsystem and added check/skip totals.
- Added explicit skip reasons for unavailable privileged or writable-temp tests.
- Added free-memory measurements before requires, after requires, and at exit.
- Added stale failure-marker cleanup after successful runs.
- Added selfcheck manual page and documented host-test limitations.
- Defined native, partial, supported, and intentionally unsupported
  compatibility levels.
- Replaced broad roadmap with kernel-first server essentials and no desktop
  scope.


1.08 - 2026-09-26 - fc8432b
--------------------------------
Shell scripting release.

- Added `sh FILE [ARG...]` and `sh -c COMMAND [NAME [ARG...]]`.
- Added positional parameters: `$0`, `$1` through `$9`, `${10}`, `$#`, `$*`,
  `$@`, and argument-preserving `"$@"`.
- Added multiline/nested `if`/`else`/`fi` and finite `for`/`do`/`done`.
- Added continuation prompts for incomplete interactive compound commands.
- Made `source FILE [ARG...]` use shell contexts with bounded nesting.
- Made script-file execution incremental and periodically yielding.
- Added numeric `exit N` propagation through kernel process exit state.
- Fixed builtin status handling and standalone source redirection/quiet mode.
- Expanded shell selfchecks and documentation.


1.07 - 2026-09-26 - 396169c
--------------------------------
Process groups and signals.

- Added process groups, `getpgid`, `setpgid`, and `waitGroup`.
- Added TERM, KILL, INT, STOP, CONT, numeric signals, and signal 0 checks.
- Added process-group signaling through negative IDs.
- Added standalone `kill` plus matching shell builtin behavior.
- STOPped processes no longer consume scheduler CPU; PID 1 cannot be stopped.
- Standardized TERM/KILL/INT exit statuses as 143/137/130.
- Changed ordinary spawns to lead new groups unless explicit PGID is supplied.


1.06 - 2026-09-26 - 2afc374
--------------------------------
Timed events and child status correctness.

- Fixed timers and timed event waits on otherwise idle machines.
- Integrated event timeout dispatch with thread scheduling.
- Changed `os.execute` to Lua 5.2 result form: `true, "exit", 0` or
  `nil, "exit", code`.
- Correctly propagated child statuses through less, man, pastebin, and time.
- Added timer, timeout, and failed-child selfchecks.


1.05 - 2026-09-26 - 9637432
--------------------------------
Filesystem-aware completion.

- Completed builtins, aliases, PATH commands, files, directories, absolute and
  relative paths, and option values following `=`.
- Escaped shell-special characters and kept directory candidates open with `/`.
- Supported completion at cursor position rather than line end only.


1.04 - 2026-09-26 - c81ae25
--------------------------------
Immutable system-update sources.

- GitHub-backed updates resolve `main` through GitHub API first.
- Release files then come from one immutable commit SHA, preventing mixed files
  when upstream changes during an update.
- Custom mirrors continue using configured URLs directly.


1.03 - 2026-09-26 - 37f3dc0
--------------------------------
Default package repository publication.

- Added hosted `apt/dists/freax` Release and empty binary-all Packages indexes.
- Clarified that repository content under `apt/` is hosted, not installed.


1.02 - 2026-09-26 - c1e4ed0
--------------------------------
bit32 compatibility.

- Uses host bit32 only when required Lua 5.2 operations exist.
- Falls back to per-process pure-Lua implementation on incomplete hosts.


1.01 - 2026-09-26 - 72730ab
--------------------------------
Service and repair fixes.

- Fixed aggregate `systemctl status` and unit listing.
- Made forced `apt install sys` repair truly re-download all eligible files.
- Updated messages left over from removed `apt sys*` commands.


1.00 - 2026-09-26 - 69bec2e
--------------------------------
First stable-series release.

- Fixed raw web-installer password input and missing Unicode dependency.
- Fixed tilde expansion, duplicate shell echo registration, head parsing and
  zero-count behavior, and sleep smoke-test regressions.
- Fixed stale systemctl response consumption, output normalization, and error
  statuses.
- Added explicit root checking to mount.
- Installed `/selfcheck.lua` through normal and web installation paths.
- Expanded installer/selfcheck documentation and coverage.
- Included final pre-release fixes from 8365fac.


0.99 - 2026-09-25 - ced6741
--------------------------------
- Restored parsing of historical passwordless shadow entries using either
  single- or double-colon forms.
- Standardized newly written passwordless entries while retaining old-disk
  compatibility.


0.98 - 2026-09-25 - 0f86756
--------------------------------
- Replaced unreliable OpenOS `term.read` password input with raw key events.
- Added printable Unicode, Enter, Backspace, and stale-event flushing.


0.97 - 2026-09-25 - f7a1e19
--------------------------------
- Recognized bare Enter/control-character results as empty web-install password.
- Improved masked password prompt formatting.


0.96 - 2026-09-25 - e4769de
--------------------------------
- Fixed empty password handling in stock OpenOS web installer.
- Correctly treated `computer.setBootAddress` returning no value as success.


0.95 - 2026-09-25 - f5dddd9
--------------------------------
OS updates became apt's virtual `sys` package.

- `apt update` refreshes package repositories and OS release metadata.
- `apt upgrade` upgrades packages and base OS together.
- Added list/show/policy/install/verify support for `sys`.
- Protected `sys` from removal and allowed forced reapplication.
- Removed separate `apt sysupdate`, `sysupgrade`, and `sysverify` commands.


0.94 - 2026-09-25 - 3a31522
--------------------------------
- Made OS replacement move old files aside, install, re-hash, and roll back on
  failure.
- Added `apt sysverify [--repair]` for installed-tree verification and repair.
- Fixed false success when OC filesystems refused overwrite-by-rename.


0.93 - 2026-09-25 - 73fe126
--------------------------------
- Fixed lazy `/dev` mounting through correct devfs proxy resolution.
- Added devfs list and isDirectory behavior.
- Bad shell substitutions now report errors without killing login shell.


0.92 - 2026-09-25 - 8f02bdd
--------------------------------
Kernel-owned multi-user security boundary.

- Added real/effective UID/GID credentials and root-only `spawnAs`.
- Made USER/LOGNAME display-only rather than authorization sources.
- Restricted machine controls, mounts, packages, installation, account changes,
  and service control to root.
- Confined non-root writes to configured home and private temp tree.
- Protected shadow reads and restricted kill/wait by credentials.
- Limited setuid behavior to su and passwd; normal exec drops effective IDs.
- Added retained child status and richer ps UID/parent/state/fd/event fields.
- Disabled removable-media autorun because kernel-phase execution bypassed
  process credentials.
- Required complete SHA256 and size metadata for repository packages.
- Rejected package symlinks until links persist across reboot.
- Preserved locally modified conffiles through `.dpkg-new`.

Compatibility breaks:
- Non-root filesystem and hardware behavior became restricted.
- Kernel autorun was removed.
- Package symlink entries stopped installing.


0.91 - 2026-09-25 - 264f54e
--------------------------------
Broad security and reliability hardening.

- Enforced fd ownership for files, networking, and redirected child stdio.
- Made syscall, standard-library, computer, I/O, and OS proxies read-only.
- Restricted shared libraries to stateless core modules.
- Hardened malformed/missing shadow handling.
- Rejected non-canonical, duplicate, traversal, truncated, or unknown manifest
  and fpkg entries.
- Added backup/rollback behavior for package status replacement.
- Prevented cross-device rename from deleting source after copy/close failure.
- Hardened installer address resolution and incomplete-install boot handling.
- Validated system-update manifests, checksum paths, and missing local files.
- Fixed shell substitutions, glob iteration, builtin exceptions, command
  substitution errors, and pipeline status handling.
- Added service cycle detection, safer stop/restart, normalized unit keys, and
  real daemon reload.
- Corrected documentation: background `&` was not implemented.


0.90 - 2026-09-19 - 20a0e5a
--------------------------------
- Allowed commands and scripts containing paths to execute correctly.
- Made PATH resolution absolute while honoring relative entries such as `.`.
- Resolved relative spawn paths against caller cwd instead of `/`.


0.89 - 2026-09-19 - 91f517e
--------------------------------
- Replaced component hard failure with sandboxed OpenOS compatibility bridge.
- Added mediated GPU, screen, keyboard, filesystem, internet, computer, and
  EEPROM access without raw component-bus authority.
- Added GPU get/maxResolution and seekable handles.


0.88 - 2026-09-19 - 3daca03
--------------------------------
- Used installed SHA256SUMS as synchronized state instead of full-system hashing.
- Reported actual changed-file download count.


0.87 - 2026-09-19 - fe141bb
--------------------------------
- Multi-match completion now lists candidates and redraws prompt/input cleanly.


0.86 - 2026-09-19 - b2b1710
--------------------------------
- Added Unicode-aware Left/Right, Home/End, Delete, and insertion editing.
- Corrected history and clipboard cursor positioning.
- Yielded during checksum scanning to avoid watchdog termination.
- Cached changed-file set between update and upgrade.


0.85 - 2026-09-19 - f88d27a
--------------------------------
- Wrapped long shell input across rows and scrolled correctly at screen bottom.
- Prevented modifiers/control keys from appearing as text.


0.84 - 2026-09-19 - 97aae58
--------------------------------
- Added generated SHA256SUMS and mksums.lua.
- Downloaded only changed OS files and verified each before installation.
- Detected stale checksum indexes and fell back to full update.
- Accepted valid zero-byte shipped files.


0.83 - 2026-09-19 - c3f6e22
--------------------------------
Web installer and package-removal safety.

- Added standalone webinstall.lua for installation from stock OpenOS.
- Added manifest download, disk selection, streaming copy, account setup,
  labeling, boot-address setup, retry/reporting, and documentation.
- Accepted legitimate zero-byte files.
- Prevented package remove/upgrade from recursively deleting shared non-empty
  directories such as /bin or /usr.


0.82 - 2026-09-19 - 4b583d0
--------------------------------
- Fixed clipboard event layouts across different OpenComputers runtimes.


0.81 - 2026-09-19 - dc76cd6
--------------------------------
- Added clipboard paste to kernel line editor.
- Queued multiline clipboard content as submitted input lines.


0.8 - 2026-09-19 - ceb6d53 / ca1a4f2
--------------------------------------------
Debian-inspired package system.

- Added streaming fpkg archives and RFC822 control metadata.
- Added Debian-style version comparison, dependencies, alternatives, Provides,
  conflicts, upgrades, and autoremove.
- Added apt, dpkg, dpkg-deb, and apt-ftparchive.
- Added package indexes, SHA256/size verification, lifecycle scripts,
  conffiles, status database, cache management, and repository tooling.
- Moved manifest OS updating behind temporary `apt sysupdate/sysupgrade` flows.
- Added Debian-style `deb` repository source lines.

Compatibility break:
- Ordinary apt commands became package-oriented; OS update temporarily moved to
  `sys*` subcommands until 0.95.


0.71 - 2026-09-19 - 66f6c4c
---------------------------------
Low-memory shared runtime.

- Compiled selected core libraries once per machine with process-dispatched
  freax/io/os proxies.
- Kept stateful/transient libraries per process for reclamation.
- Added computer, unicode, and pure-Lua bit32 require shims.
- Deferred devfs and authentication loading to reduce boot memory.
- Corrected unsupported reader-function load attempt to table.concat/load.
- Added robust internet-card discovery and fd-backed internet streams.
- Made Ctrl+C kill foreground command trees with status 130.
- Added kernel log ring, installer/selfcheck diagnostics, and dmesg output.
- Prevented manual second systemd instance and surprise relogin.
- Added update cache-busting and shell REPL pcall protection.


0.7 - 2026-09-18 - ddadb4e
--------------------------------
Large OpenOS compatibility and utility expansion.

- Ported/expanded ls, cp, mv, grep, find, tree, ps, dmesg, less, head, du,
  mount, rm, rmdir, edit, and many related tools/options.
- Added cd, clear, rc, set, source, unset, useradd, and userdel.
- Added actual mounts, read-only mounts, process-handle APIs, io.popen, improved
  pipes/TTY streams, and broad OpenOS-compatible libraries.
- Replaced shell execution path with reusable lib/sh.lua.
- Added lazy devfs framework, PATH completion, temporary autorun support,
  terminal GPU/ANSI methods, and process views.
- Fixed event/Ctrl+C handling, temp files, command lookup, sleep interruption,
  shutdown handling, and many command exit/option bugs.


0.6 - 2026-09-18 - d960be0
--------------------------------
Accounts, installer, FHS layout, services, and updater.

- Added passwd/shadow accounts, login, passwd, su, masked passwords, and
  getty-style sessions.
- Reworked installer into one full 4K-streamed low-memory install path.
- Added target verification, drive labels, account DB generation, and /home
  preservation; stopped shipping live credential databases.
- Reorganized repository to mirror installed FHS tree.
- Added PID 1 service manager, systemctl, unit startup, console fallback, and
  service status.
- Made scheduler resume live processes each tick so daemons progress when idle.
- Added Unicode-safe keyboard input and many login/terminal fixes.
- Added VERSION, manifest-driven installation, and first in-game apt updater.
- Removed destructive fresh-media demo wipe.

Compatibility break:
- Flat media layout moved to FHS, with temporary boot fallbacks for old media.


0.5 - 2026-09-17 - 6d6c45f
--------------------------------
- Unified visible branding/version as Freax 0.5.
- Added reliable exit-code propagation and typeahead while waiting.
- Added file-backed stdio duplication and inherited cwd/environment.
- Added virtual RAM symlinks, ln, man, and initial manual pages.
- Symlinks intentionally disappeared on reboot, matching OpenOS behavior.


Prototype 0.1 kernel / 0.2 userland - 2026-09-17 - 8f2c472
----------------------------------------------------------------
- Initial coroutine scheduler and private process environments.
- Added kernel-mediated hardware, VFS/mounts, pipes, fd I/O, networking, and
  terminal support.
- Added broad first command set and early shell pipelines, redirects, boolean
  chains, aliases, source, foreground waits, and job scaffolding.
- Kernel and userland reported different prototype versions; no VERSION file
  existed yet.
